1. e4 c5 2. Nf3 d6 3. d4 cxd4 4. Nxd4 Nf6 5. Nc3 Nc6 6. Bg5 e6 7. Qd2 a6 8.
O-O-O h6 9. Be3 Bd7 10. f4 Be7 11. Kb1 Qc7 12. Qe1 b5 13. Bd3 O-O 14. Rf1 Rac8
15. Qg3 Nxd4 16. Bxd4 b4 17. Ne2 Bb5 18. Rc1 Rfd8 19. f5 e5 20. Be3 Kf8 21. Qh3
Qb7 22. g4 Nxe4 23. Bxb5 Qxb5 24. Ng3 Nc3+ $1 25. Ka1 Qa5 $2 ({Both players
had only ten minutes to reach the time control but what a pity that Hort did
not play the beautiful line that he tought of during dinner that evening:} 
25... Qa4 $1 26. bxc3 Rxc3 27. f6 Ra3 $1 28. fxe7+ Ke8 $3 29. exd8=Q+ Kxd8 30.
Kb1 Rxa2 31. Bb6+ {(with the black king queen on a5 this would win)} Ke8 32.
Bd4 exd4 33. Rce1+ Kd8 34. Qh4+ f6 35. Re8+ Kxe8 36. Qh5+ Kd8 {and White will
mated}) 26. bxc3 Rxc3 27. f6 Ra3 28. fxe7+ Kxe7 29. Kb1 Rxa2 $2 ({Stockfish 16:
} 29... Qd5 $1 $19) 30. Bd4 exd4 31. Rxf7+ $1 Kxf7 32. Qf1+ Kg8 33. Qc4+ d5 34.
Qxa2 Qb5 35. Rd1 a5 36. Qb2 a4 37. Qxd4 b3 38. c4 Qb7 39. Nf5 a3 40. Re1 a2+ $2
({Stockfish 16:} 40... b2 41. Ka2 Kh8 $11) 41. Ka1 Rb8 $2 ({Stockfish 16:} 
41... b2+ 42. Qxb2 Qxb2+ 43. Kxb2 dxc4 44. Re2 $14) 42. Qxd5+ {Sources:
bulletin; BCM, December 1977, p552} 1-0

