Bb6 35. Kf1 h5 36. Rd6 Rg5 37. h4 Bxe3 38. hxg5 hxg4 39. Rxg6+ Kf7 40. Rdd6 Re8
41. Rdf6+ Ke7 {Sources: bulletin; BCM, December 1977, p552} ({After} 41... Ke7
{Lambert offered a draw which Kotov declined, pointing out that he could win by
} 42. Re6+ (42. Rg7+ Kd8 43. Rd6+ Kc8 44. Rxa6 Kb8 45. a5 g3 46. Rb6+ Bxb6 47.
axb6 e3 $19) (42. Rxa6 g3 $19) (42. Rd6 $1 g3 43. Rge6+ {draws}) 42... Kd7 43.
Rxe8 Kxe8 ({However, Black should not play 43...Kxe8 but} 43... g3 $1 {and
White would have had to resign.}) 44. Re6+ {and 45 Rxe4. Lambert thereupon
resigned.}) 1-0

